# Tracer: anonymous-function declared return-set validation
#
# Before (incorrectly verified):
# fn(x R) N {x}(1 / 2) $in N
# Former behavior: the literal trusted N even though its body x only had the R carrier.
#
# Now (verified):
fn(x R) R {x}(1 / 2) = 1 / 2
# Current behavior: a body that belongs to its declared return set remains well-defined.
#
# Boundary: fn(x R) N {x} is rejected before application because x $in N is not verified.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/_internal/regression/anonymous_fn_return_set_validation.lit
# Implementation: src/verify/verify_obj_well_defined/sets.rs
